// A lambda that captures a live local cannot cross a thread boundary, and
// the uniqueness check says so in the words it already had: the capture is a
// field, the list is reachable from the sender's own local as well as from
// the lambda, and that is exactly the shape `rt_check_unique` refuses.
//
// This is the whole of why `spawn` keeps taking a function and its
// arguments rather than a closure (docs/closures-decision.md §6): with a
// closure the ordinary case would be this trap, while `spawn f(x)` states
// the captures as arguments and the move checker sees them by name.
//
// A lambda with NO captures is immortal and crosses freely -- corpus/core/1104.
interface Get { int of(); }

Chan<Get> inbox = Chan<Get>(2);
List<int> xs = [1, 2, 3];
send(inbox, () => xs.size());
